# Frontend feature

## When to use
- New panel in `app/sections/`, hook, or dashboard data slice
- Consume new `/api/dashboard/*` or related endpoints

## Inspect first
- `app/page.tsx` layout grid and existing panels
- `app/contexts/V3DashboardDataContext.tsx` and `app/lib/v3DashboardFetchers.ts`
- `app/types/index.ts` for shared types
- `app/rules/v3-rules.tsx` if changing pipeline/product copy on `/rules`
- `getApiBase()` behavior (browser vs server); production API via Vercel env `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`

## Steps
1. Add typed fetcher in `v3DashboardFetchers.ts` (or extend existing loader).
2. Wire slice in `V3DashboardDataProvider` with `loading` / `error` / `refresh`.
3. Build section component using `Card` / `CardHeader`; keep JSX presentational.
4. Place panel on page grid; match spacing and responsive columns.
5. Use `'use client'` only on files that need interactivity.

## Verification
- [ ] `cd frontend && npm run build`
- [ ] `npm run lint` if touching many files
- [ ] Browser check: loading, error, and refresh paths
- [ ] API base works in dev (backend on :3000, frontend on :3001)
